# Replace with the URL assigned to the NEW Render service.
@baseUrl = https://your-new-service.onrender.com
# Local alternative: http://localhost:8080
# Define idToken in git-ignored http-client.private.env.json, not this file.

### Public database health: expect 200 with database=connected
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health

### Public flowers: expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/flowers?page=0&size=1

### Application health: expect 200 with status=UP
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### Missing authentication: expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth-debug

### Blank token: expect 400 (401 suggests different deployed security settings)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/google
Content-Type: application/json

{"idToken":""}

# For real sign-in, Android sends a fresh Google ID token in the JSON body.
# Protected requests use Authorization: Bearer <that same Google ID token>.


### Real Google sign-in: expect 200 and a registered userId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/google
Content-Type: application/json

{"idToken":"{{idToken}}"}

### Current user: expect 200 after sign-in (no X-User-Id header)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Protected quote retrieval: expect 200 with a valid token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
